-- ============================================================================
-- Seed: demo contributors and power_logs
--
-- Per CLAUDE.md decision 6 ("Seed heavily in M1... empty dashboards look
-- broken"), this seeds realistic event-based power_logs for 10 LGAs spread
-- across different states/regions:
--   Lagos/Ikeja, Lagos/Alimosho, FCT/Abuja Municipal, Kano/Kano Municipal,
--   Rivers/Port Harcourt, Oyo/Ibadan North, Enugu/Enugu North,
--   Kaduna/Kaduna North, Akwa Ibom/Uyo, Borno/Maiduguri.
--
-- power_logs.user_id is a NOT NULL FK to auth.users (ON DELETE CASCADE), so
-- this requires real auth.users rows, not fake UUIDs. Section 003a inserts
-- synthetic anonymous auth users (is_anonymous = true, no email/password,
-- matching what Supabase's own anonymous sign-in writes) directly via SQL,
-- which bypasses RLS as expected for seed data and fires the
-- on_auth_user_created trigger from 0001_init.sql, auto-creating an empty
-- public.profiles row per user. Section 003b then backfills display_name/
-- state_id/lga_id/area_id on those rows (the trigger only sets id).
--
-- Section 003c inserts the actual logs: 4-5 contributors per LGA (42 users
-- total), each an alternating on/off event sequence (never two consecutive
-- same-status logs for the same user+area, matching CLAUDE.md decision 1 —
-- events, not durations), spread over a random 14-26 day window per user
-- ending at generation time, with irregular multi-hour gaps (jittered, never
-- periodic) biased per LGA by a rough "uptime_bias" texture knob so the ten
-- areas don't all read identically. ~15-25% of 'on' logs are tagged with a
-- power_source (generator/inverter/solar) to exercise decision 4's grid-only
-- filtering; 'off' logs are left untagged. source is always 'manual'.
--
-- Does NOT touch outage_intervals (that's the M2 scheduled job's job) or
-- fault_reports/fault_confirmations/discos/admin_audit_log (out of scope).
--
-- Re-runnable: 003a/003b are guarded by ON CONFLICT (id) against the primary
-- keys of auth.users/public.profiles. power_logs has no unique constraint in
-- 0001_init.sql (consecutive-duplicate prevention is deliberately an
-- app-layer concern, not a DB one), so 003c instead guards with a
-- NOT EXISTS (user_id, logged_at) check — a natural dedup key for this
-- deterministic, pre-generated dataset.
-- ============================================================================

